1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,400
What happens when we send electrons, one at a time, toward two tiny openings?

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:12,000
Each electron arrives as a single spot. But something surprising happens as the spots build up.

3
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:18,600
Together, they form an interference pattern, revealing the wave-like behavior of quantum particles.

4
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:26,800
When the experiment reveals which slit an electron takes, that interference disappears.

5
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:36,600
Not because a human mind controls reality, but because quantum behavior is different from everyday experience.
